    <description>Quick Action screen flow reachable from any open Opportunity stage. Captures Loss Reason (required), Competitor Outcome, and Notes (required); sets AF_LostApprovalStatus__c = Pending and AF_ApprovalRecipient__c = the Owner&apos;s Manager, then submits for approval — StageName is never touched here, which is what keeps &apos;s request-and-approve path deadlock-free. Deliberately does NOT send the approver notification (email or Custom Notification) itself anymore — that logic moved to AF_FL_Opp_ApprovalRequested, a record-triggered flow on the Pending status change, matching the pattern already used for Approved/Rejected. Reason: this is a Screen Flow, and Screen Flows cannot be invoked programmatically (Flow.Interview.start explicitly rejects process type Screen Flow), so any notification logic embedded here is untestable via Apex and never fires for anything other than a live UI click — it also wouldn&apos;t fire for the case where AF_LostApprovalStatus__c is set to Pending some other way. A record-triggered flow reacting to the field value itself covers every path that sets Pending, not just this screen.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
